<title>FINLAND: FINNISH BONDS CLOSE HIGHER, GAP OVER BUND NARROWS.</title>
<headline>FINNISH BONDS CLOSE HIGHER, GAP OVER BUND NARROWS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonds outperformed German Bunds</p>
<p>in improving sentiment after Swedish riksbank trimmed its repo</p>
<p>rate by 25 basis points to 4.35 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>Money rates fell and the State Treasury raised 1.35 billion</p>
<p>markka in its auction of T-bills -- over a billion for the first</p>
<p>time since October 1.</p>
<p>Operators said there was scope for the gap over Germany to</p>
<p>narrow more at the long end as long as Germany is strong.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe that 50 to 40 basis points is sustainable, that</p>
<p>leaves room for narrowing (in EMU),&quot; one analyst said.</p>
<p>-- Roland Moller, Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0245</p>
</text>
